  "releaseNotes": "Video recording: the shutter can now record as well as shoot. CaptureModes is the whole switch — pass\n\t\t\tno modes (or one) and there is no mode selector, no microphone is ever asked for and nothing changes,\n\t\t\texactly like the zoom, quality and timer bars. With video mode on, the pills above the shutter pick what\n\t\t\tthe button does, the shutter turns red and becomes a stop button while recording, and an indicator over\n\t\t\tthe viewfinder shows the elapsed time and how much of the limit is left. MaxVideoDuration defaults to a\n\t\t\tminute; the limit is not enforced in the browser but reported, so ending by time and ending by the\n\t\t\tshutter take exactly the same path.\n\n\t\t\tThe component does NOT hold the recording. A photo is handed over whole because a photo is small; a\n\t\t\tminute of video is tens of megabytes, and a component that accumulated it would be deciding, for the\n\t\t\tconsumer, that all of it fits in memory. So OnVideoChunk delivers slices as they are produced — the next\n\t\t\tone is not produced until the handler has completed, so a slow consumer slows delivery instead of piling\n\t\t\tup — and OnVideoRecorded closes with the totals. Whether those slices become a file, rows in a local\n\t\t\tdatabase or blocks pushed to storage is the consumer's business, the same division as with a photo.\n\n\t\t\tRecording is MP4 only, and where the browser cannot encode it the mode is not offered at all rather than\n\t\t\tfailing when the shutter is pressed. The microphone is requested when the user picks video mode, not\n\t\t\twhen the camera loads, and it is released on the way out; refusing it records a silent video instead of\n\t\t\tno video. OnVideoPosterCaptured hands over the first frame as an ordinary JPEG photo — the frame the\n\t\t\tuser was looking at when they pressed record — with no flash and no torch. Digital zoom is suspended\n\t\t\twhile recording: the crop is a CSS transform over the preview and never reaches the recorded track, so\n\t\t\tpresets beyond the camera's own zoom would promise a framing the file does not have. Custom\n\t\t\tICameraCapture implementations gain five members; a backend that answers false to SupportsRecordingAsync\n\t\t\tkeeps the previous behaviour.\n\n\t\t\tA still can also be taken while a recording runs, from a button beside the shutter: an ordinary photo\n\t\t\tthrough OnPhotoCaptured, with no relation to the video, because the frame worth keeping is rarely the\n\t\t\tframe the recording ends on. In the browser the two never collide — a photo is the current frame copied\n\t\t\tto a canvas and the recorder is reading the track. AllowPhotoWhileRecording turns it off where the\n\t\t\tbackend cannot do both at once, and SnapshotContent replaces the icon.",
